00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.640
formulating practice if you buy cosmetic
ingredients from a manufacturer then on

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.840
their product data sheet they usually
tell you the recommended percentages for

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.879
a particular ingredient
so with niacinamide for example it's

00:04:10.879 --> 00:04:15.760
usually recommended at 0.5 to 5 percent
with l ascorbic acid it's recommended

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.880
at five to fifteen percent
the reason there's an upper limit on

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.079
these percentages isn't because they're
trying to trick you

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:25.199
and get more money out of you because if
you think about it the ingredient

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:28.240
suppliers are actually going to make
more money and sell more product

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.320
if they get cosmetic formulators to use
more of their active ingredients

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.919
the reason is that scientific studies
have already found really good effects

00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:38.400
at these levels
and they haven't actually found better

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.440
effects at higher levels the higher
levels have never been used in

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.280
scientific studies
there's no real reason to use them if

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.280
you're looking for skin brightening
because

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.479
it actually hasn't been tested and in
general if you have

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:53.919
a high percentage the more likely it is
you'll have side effects

00:04:53.919 --> 00:04:57.840
so the likely irritation and stress to
your skin probably isn't worth it for

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.080
that
theoretical extra benefit so you might

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.080
be gaining this much irritation and only
this much extra effect or even no extra

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.560
effect
an analogy is food so there's going to

