with the product but there's still a ton

00:09:05.279 --> 00:09:08.959
of problems with this
so firstly a scoop is what we call a

00:09:08.959 --> 00:09:12.000
volumetric measurement so you're seeing
how much stuff you can cram into a

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.959
particular volume
volumetric measurements of items are

00:09:14.959 --> 00:09:18.880
never really that reliable
so we know this from everyday life so if

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:22.320
you go and get a box of salads some
places will pack it full of salad

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:25.360
and some places will give you like a
couple of leaves that expand to fill the

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.680
whole container
and so you get wildly different amounts

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.760
of salad you get very different amounts
of fullness from that salad even though

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.240
both
are a box even when it's something

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:38.480
relatively solid like let's say
strawberries you still get a really wide

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:42.399
range of amounts because you can have
large strawberries you can chop them up

00:09:42.399 --> 00:09:46.000
into finely diced strawberries and you
can fit a lot more of that finely diced

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.279
strawberry into that cup
even with something like a powder where

00:09:49.279 --> 00:09:53.440
the range of sizes is pretty small
you can still get things like a tightly

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.480
packed cup of flour versus a loosely
packed cup of flour

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.560
so even with this sort of powder where
it looks like it's all the same size

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.000
if you zoom in there's actually a whole
bunch of different sizes

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.200
so if you have a jar of powder with
different sizes of powder which they

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.959
almost always have then what's going to
happen is that the bigger particles tend

00:10:10.959 --> 00:10:13.920
to stay at the top
and the smaller particles filter down to

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.959
the bottom and so
when you're up the top you're scooping

00:10:16.959 --> 00:10:19.360
up bigger particles which means you get
less mass

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.800
in your scoop when you get down to the
bottom then you end up with a more

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.920
tightly packed powder
and so you end up with a greater

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:30.800
percentage and with things like skincare
that percentage is based on mass not on

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.680
volume so it's not like
five percent is one scoop per 20 scoops

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.800
it is one mass per 20 masses and so
that's going to make a difference

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:45.040
now in my diy vitamin c recipe i did
give a volumetric measurement as an

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.839
approximation
and that's because i realized that not

00:10:47.839 --> 00:10:51.680
everyone has scales at home
and so giving an approximate volumetric

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.600
measurement is probably better than
nothing

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.360
better than add a small amount anyway
there's also a really wide range of

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.120
l-ascorbic acid concentrations that are
both safe and effective so between five

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:04.959
and twenty percent if you aim for ten
percent that means you have a hundred

00:11:04.959 --> 00:11:07.760
percent leeway either way
and so if you're measuring a large

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.720
amount like a whole teaspoon of powder
then you have a lot of leeway it's

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.800
really hard to be out by a hundred
percent

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.560
and that's one of my biggest issues with
these powders they recommend that you do

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.440
it per dose so
each time you put it on your face you

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:25.440
measure out the small amount
with my diy serum you are making 20 mL

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.839
at a time
and so when you're measuring a larger

00:11:27.839 --> 00:11:30.800
amount you have a smaller percentage
error

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:34.640
and this is the reason i've never
recommended making up your vitamin c per

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.040
